    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12128" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cȳmătĭum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cūm-</span></b> ) or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-on</span></b> , ii,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυμάτιον</span> (a small
		wave); in architecture, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The volute of an Ionic column</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 3, 5,
				7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 1,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A channel, a waved moulding, an ogee</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 3, 5,
				10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 3,
			6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 3, 8</span></i>;
			4, 6, 2; <i><span class="en">Tert. Idol. 8</span></i>.</div>
